==[[Range/Lore|The Range's lore assets]]==
===[[Range/Lore/EP4|Episode 4]]===
*{{AC|file=KAYO Audio Log Istanbul Mission Complete.mp3}} ''(For the entire transcription amongst the agents, see [[Range/Lore/EP4#Cypher's_Office|Range/Lore/EP4 → v4.07 → Cypher's Office]].)''
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone17.mp3}} "[[Brimstone]]. I've completed my audio analysis of the interrogation. My conclusion is the same as yours; our [[Fade|house guest]] is not the enemy, if anything, she is an ally. An ally with enormous potential. Her suspicion of [[VALORANT Protocol|VALORANT]] is understandable given the state of our world, but if we can find a mutually beneficial agreement, I foresee great things for us all. I support her recruitment. Just keep her away from my servers."
*{{AC|file=Cypher Interrogation Audio.mp3}} ''(For the entire transcription between Cypher and [[Fade]], see [[Range/Lore/EP4#Cypher's_Office_2|Range/Lore/EP4 → v4.08 → Cypher's Office]].)''
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone22.mp3}} "Brimstone. We're out of those little coffee pod things in the common room. I don't use them, but when they're gone, everyone starts drinking my tea. And please understand, it's very expensive tea. Thank you."

===[[Range/Lore/EP5|Episode 5]]===
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone28.mp3}} "It's me. The soldiers we fought on Omega belong to an organization called [[Atlas]]. Details are hard to come by, Atlas operates far outside the public sphere. They have dealings with [[Kingdom Industries|Omega Kingdom]], but as far as I can tell they are a separate business. And no official connection with [[VALORANT Legion|Omega VALORANT]]. Bit of a shock, given how they teamed up with the [[Omega Viper|enemy Viper]] to push us back. If there's an arrangement, it's a whisper. In the end we know their name, but we do not know who they are. When I find out, I will call."

===[[Range/Lore/EP6|Episode 6]]===
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone44.mp3}} "Hello, Brimstone. I have 'concerns' about our dear [[Fade|dream seer]]. Er, not the usual ones- she's not sleeping well. I see her up and wandering at all hours, afflicted in her unique way, always troubled, I can tell. Her power is an asset but not at the cost of her life. Is there something we can do? She is not one to ask for help, so I will ask in her stead."
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone54.mp3}} "Brimstone! I'm calling you, again, to request more servers. The surveillance library is near capacity. Compressing image and sound quality is out of the question. And no, I cannot free up space by purging the archives you claim are no longer valuable! It is all valuable! The only option is more servers! Don't make me delete anything, please Brimstone! I beg you, please!"

===[[Range/Lore/EP7|Episode 7]]===
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone66.mp3}} "Brim, card game tonight. So far it's the usual group, plus [[Astra]] and [[Sage]]. Oh and, uh, apparently [[Omen]] wants to watch... just go with it. If you're in, let me know."

===[[Range/Lore/EP8|Episode 8]]===
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone74.mp3}} "Brimstone, I found him! [[Omen]]'s in Edinburgh. Seems he was after a journal of some kind, one that belonged to our dear friends at [[Hourglass]]. I have confirmation that there was a disturbance near the library, but we know who won. Wait, wait! Hold on. Omen's checking in now... he's met [[Clove|someone]] he says you'll want to meet. Hmhm, I did always want to go to Scotland!"

===[[Range/Lore/V25|Season 2025]]===
*{{AC|file=VoicemailBrimstone104.mp3}} "Brimstone, don't ask me how I know, but an alarming number of agents still use "1234" as their password. This is not acceptable! I suggest we run my data security course again. I shortened it by twelve slides following your rather pointed feedback. Say the word, I'll see it done."

